  "slug": "plantpredict",
  "name": "PlantPredict",
  "url": "https://mcp.plantpredict.terabase.energy/",
  "description": "PlantPredict is Terabase Energy's cloud-based solar energy yield modeling platform, used by developers, EPCs, asset owners, and financiers to design and simulate the performance of utility-scale PV power plants. This connector lets Claude work directly inside your PlantPredict account to help with project and prediction management, plant design, and performance analysis.\nWith this connector, Claude can create and manage projects and predictions, configure power plant designs (blocks, arrays, DC/AC ratios), search and attach weather data, work with module and inverter equipment libraries, run yield simulations (including 3D terrain-aware backtracking, shade, and transposition calculations), and retrieve summary results, detailed outputs, and generated reports. All actions run under your own PlantPredict login and respect your account's existing permissions.\nTypical uses include comparing design scenarios for a bid, pulling P50/P90 energy results for a project, checking imported weather data for quality issues, and keeping module, inverter, and weather libraries up to date without leaving Claude.",
